{"title":"2012 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For distinct positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/c/d8c3c998e62221622912aabcadd56c8f9f05c25a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b &lt; 2012$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" />, define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/2/07254b24b1c3168cfbf6984fa9fc22b1aa0fb6df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" /> to be the number of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/6/7767ea89a744ac304878a5f9504eb78140ca1566.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le k &lt; 2012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" /> such that the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/d/f4d0d7039a400779d0c3013db5ed5a4950068462.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ak$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> divided by 2012 is greater than that of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/c/8dcceb5127d10665924b2e5b1f32de1cd53d8fac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$bk$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> divided by 2012.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/2/07254b24b1c3168cfbf6984fa9fc22b1aa0fb6df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> range over all pairs of distinct positive integers less than 2012.  Determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>First we'll show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/9/c895fef1826e6844af9e75623545ec153084e06c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S \\geq 502$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" />, then we'll find an example <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e24c43456d95b5ab8d4f2f8f85a644e98b7ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> that have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/9/ee9735ecd591eb6f0b0043b1d726f92e5bc29ae5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a, b)=502$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/d/f5d3dead9cb8d5f6327c737e014850be7a29d0f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> be the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/d/f4d0d7039a400779d0c3013db5ed5a4950068462.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ak$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> is divided by 2012, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/d/c5dd4a48fae40d106f05aa536bdbebd1f0195842.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"11\" /> be defined similarly for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/c/8dcceb5127d10665924b2e5b1f32de1cd53d8fac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$bk$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />. First, we know that, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/2/c32460fc78db10d7475e55493bf9b0dbf2fdbdf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k &gt; y_k &gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/d/ccd347893d50bfc7c6ed33429c089be3a5b75163.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{2012-k} \\equiv a(2012-k) \\equiv 2012-ak \\equiv 2012-x_k \\pmod {2012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"477\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/a/1ca4d529aa5b5bf48aa430afc4b813e5e14e5302.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_{2012-k} \\equiv 2012-y_k \\pmod {2012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"255\" height=\"20\" />. This implies that, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e11e619dd0ed437a7b5122a61044c93afe584e32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2012 - x_k \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/f/ecf7653bb6b5238eb2a3248ac6b566d4cb5bc7b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2012 -y_k \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b8914f11b686bf531d218882cf1da8a83379a40e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{2012-k} &lt; y_{2012-k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"132\" height=\"13\" />. Similarly, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/2/4b2a598ffc54a74e9bd0843662eb54a0ac65c4da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt; x_k &lt; y_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d138f83d45e47300552dba46d97007f3864e876.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{2012-k} &gt; y_{2012-k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"132\" height=\"13\" />, establishing a one-to-one correspondence between the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/2/4b2c55b40532b09f52f25fe454f0da021a91f995.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k &lt; y_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is the number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/0/1b04ba46847eb96ebb0791cae5a91b32b359c5cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k \\neq y_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/a/54a45bbe49a1a45d0d1000b6479e84b803b8eef1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_k \\neq 0 \\neq x_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/8/7c83590f44a17752bba64d3ebdd89d0657d1950f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S \\geq \\frac{1}{2}n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"37\" />. Now I'll show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/7/2473bc89a3a109b6c4054dac60ad1c29f7c7bc03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 1004$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/2/e62f226e197ac85d308048ff86eedb6159733e96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$gcd(k, 2012)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" />, then I'll show you that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/0/1b04ba46847eb96ebb0791cae5a91b32b359c5cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k \\neq y_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" />. This is actually pretty clear; assume that's not true and set up a congruence relation:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/5524877fffb98e093cb52f75df633560c110c2d5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ak \\equiv bk \\pmod {2012}\\]\" width=\"168\" height=\"18\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is relatively prime to 2012, it is invertible mod 2012, so we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/8/738ca39298d7ad6b27ddfc464348405117e5c2f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\equiv b \\pmod {2012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/c/dfc4b963e98e39d714564e4c3c037186312b339e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; a, b &lt;2012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"118\" height=\"16\" />, this means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abd2c942ae299fd26e18d0ca5d390a7ca4a8c34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, which the problem doesn't allow, thus contradiction, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/0/1b04ba46847eb96ebb0791cae5a91b32b359c5cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k \\neq y_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" />. Additionally, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/2/e62f226e197ac85d308048ff86eedb6159733e96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$gcd(k, 2012)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/7562039c1d3ef30c5e61509aadf220c146b6b456.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k \\neq 0 \\neq y_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" />, then based on what we know about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> from the previous paragraph, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is at least as large as the number of k relatively prime to 2012. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/d/a0dd11fa5a0fa3092992ecdd3f3fcb7188d30712.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq \\phi(2012) = \\phi(503*4) = 1004$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"262\" height=\"20\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/9/c895fef1826e6844af9e75623545ec153084e06c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S \\geq 502$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>To show 502 works, consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/f/11f9bca6aad4c523b2aa4b0b68e880360f3fe313.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b)=(1006, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" />. For all even <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/0/3e07c4e1a8cdd4cfb7aa48816fad3dfcf5487521.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />, so it doesn't count towards <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/2/f02eaba2438d544236e6e060c6f5082dca38851e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1006, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />. Additionally, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/7/b67a16e597403702644083b3db2e17321b10822f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 503, 503*3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"122\" height=\"16\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/e/85e48b7dea1e2b39fd24776387ffc10db1aa4c63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k = y_k = 1006$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"119\" height=\"16\" />, so the only number that count towards <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/2/f02eaba2438d544236e6e060c6f5082dca38851e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1006, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /> are the odd numbers not divisible by 503. There are 1004 such numbers. However, for all such odd k not divisible by 503 (so numbers relatively prime to 2012), we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/7562039c1d3ef30c5e61509aadf220c146b6b456.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k \\neq 0 \\neq y_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/e/9ae767f40ed800d0de3a7e2057ccd9eea1381107.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2012-k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"68\" height=\"13\" /> is also relatively prime to 2012. Since under those conditions exactly one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/9/999dd1c577071f0a176800c80b4dd1dba78bcd2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k &gt; y_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d138f83d45e47300552dba46d97007f3864e876.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{2012-k} &gt; y_{2012-k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"132\" height=\"13\" /> is true, we have at most 1/2 of the 1004 possible k actually count to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/2/f02eaba2438d544236e6e060c6f5082dca38851e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1006, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/b/fab4e28aae6acd7de13176f02defcdb040eaac5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1004}{2} = 502 \\geq f(1006, 2) \\geq S \\geq 502$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"282\" height=\"37\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/7/417bdeca4614c0e4902e1549086d8d7ea644c938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=502$\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/2/7d24f286d3c10a5f3c67127c60d99829e041925c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ak \\equiv r_{a} \\pmod{2012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67a0197bad1e72752700f33b7b3f3053269cd625.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$bk \\equiv r_{b} \\pmod{2012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"18\" />. Notice that this means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/7/327d2b6d10f615e5177dfe00cff8c23e74120b30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(2012 - k) \\equiv 2012 - r_{a} \\pmod{2012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"289\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/1/4016611650fc25182b690a8b270b057fb1ab61d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b(2012 - k) \\equiv 2012 - r_{b} \\pmod{2012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"286\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, for every value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/8/738e6d1ddf0a9f3acdccd184553a5893c2aa3d88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_{a} &gt; r_{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"12\" />, there is a value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/9/c799b5621315703b406d44a619b42d15c990d961.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_{b} &gt; r_{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"12\" />. Therefore, we merely have to calculate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> times the number of values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/f/1ef707c81be0a7eaba48818a91dc3824fc9a914d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_{a} \\neq r_{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/3/ff3457ad2360d5798c6b29db487ba1d42df5d7ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_{a} \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nHowever, the answer is NOT <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26bd476c23362090784d030e377117c4d732aeac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(2012) = 1006$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"123\" height=\"37\" />! This is because we must count the cases where the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> makes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/9/e99c37d69a12ab56b665a5909717227d92e718e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_{a} = r_{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"10\" /> or where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/9/89939859360077a4151cd3747e010f6857b83875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_{a} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nSo, let's start counting.\n</p><p><br />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is even, we have either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/4/a14e41c87c11ea67b8cd379f79b84b0f5ff0dd12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\equiv 0 \\pmod{1006}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/8/838f918a264b580376a45174347bd49d876a584e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a - b \\equiv 0 \\pmod{1006}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"170\" height=\"18\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6eff4bf6b29530e74ff975195fdba99b60e21eab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 1006$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/5/df57f2d4ab75fb117b8a3f4e8de45360aa15d237.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = b + 1006$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"14\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/9/3197521069d117debac49e2d2040cc5949184536.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1005$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> even values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> (which is all the possible even values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, since the two above requirements don't put any bounds on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> at all).\n</p><p><br />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is odd, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/5/d65172b70e527733a633aeaa3259dd65fd545afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 503$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/a/afac87e48c4f9ed3abd9f455a33c0ce379e8cbd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 503 \\cdot 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78ed257fb978e79adaea96ce64bd618d289162d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\equiv 0 \\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/5/7d552c5a68da9f884e05b3f823724c3888a29c27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\equiv b \\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" />. Otherwise, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/c/62c7a3e890710bb69798928cc41aa266243a6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ak \\equiv 0 \\pmod{2012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/3/1934b67f69fb923636223c9a340e1f410e83e989.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ak \\equiv bk \\pmod{2012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" />, which is impossible to satisfy, given the domain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/7/d27b9d94c2e294a72ee05555fcd494cc653c106c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b &lt; 2012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />. So, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nIn total, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/2/71225df99fff67bc2d614b1907794662e815596c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 1005 = 1007$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"128\" height=\"14\" /> values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> which makes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/9/e99c37d69a12ab56b665a5909717227d92e718e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_{a} = r_{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/9/89939859360077a4151cd3747e010f6857b83875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_{a} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/5/495af04be8e5e57fff07df18f1a3f1a93f5f6dda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2011 - 1007 = 1004$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"155\" height=\"13\" /> values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/f/1ef707c81be0a7eaba48818a91dc3824fc9a914d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_{a} \\neq r_{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/3/ff3457ad2360d5798c6b29db487ba1d42df5d7ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_{a} \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"17\" />. Thus, by our reasoning above, our solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/4/c04a5cf8244bb49fb389f2c6e47ca0b801a8087b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 1004 = \\boxed{502}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"126\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nSolution by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/9/4696a579baa87a4e385fe39c397b54d94d70557b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{\\underline{Invoker}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The key insight in this problem is noticing that when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/d/f4d0d7039a400779d0c3013db5ed5a4950068462.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ak$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> is higher than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/c/8dcceb5127d10665924b2e5b1f32de1cd53d8fac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$bk$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598ca19b1bdf3ce16c4a80cf421142f151f71052.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(2012-k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" /> is lower than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/5/0d527c39bba68573cb4c45a412ba518e08054a86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b(2012-k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" />, except at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef1b2ff8d4401a9eecc589aae9c5cf959aa2c222.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> residues*. Also, they must be equal many times. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/887139c4a207b912e4188fa9f3f27898b33a25fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2012=2^2*503$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />. We should have multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/3/7d3817057d16af06717c17f3803fa0d447eb2347.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$503$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. After trying all three pairs and getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/3/7d3817057d16af06717c17f3803fa0d447eb2347.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$503$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> as our answer, we win. But look at the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/5/a852d686e9175debe363eb9c3abd503a554d685f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" /> idea. What if we just took <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and plugged it in with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/2/2524e7efcb927db9f32af0f14bd63706b4aa9028.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1006$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />?\nWe get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/6/f563574744d6a2d6761415d8edfe3b33182be38d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$502$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<pre>--<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Va2010&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:Va2010 (page does not exist)\">Va2010</a> 11:12, 28 April 2012 (EDT)va2010\n</pre>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Say that the problem is a race track with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/8/f48f95ec89b6c50220ecbbbb6130586135db8ff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2012$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> spots. To intersect the most, we should get next to each other a lot so the negation is high. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/887139c4a207b912e4188fa9f3f27898b33a25fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2012=2^2*503$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />, we intersect at a lot of multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/3/7d3817057d16af06717c17f3803fa0d447eb2347.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$503$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\">USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO\" title=\"2012 USAJMO\">2012 USAJMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2012 USAJMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=176&amp;year=2012\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017231046\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.056 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.077 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 671/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1326/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 22042/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   16.777      1 -total\n 69.37%   11.639      1 Template:USAJMO_newbox\n 28.75%    4.823      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11060:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017231046 and revision id 194815. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}